  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the most favorable outcome of each lottery (its least probable positive outcome) and prefers the one with the higher monetary value (6000 > 3000, so prefer B). However, the individual’s reasoning focuses on the probability of winning anything at all and explicitly favors the higher probability (0.2% > 0.1%), even with a lower reward. The individual does not highlight or prioritize the 6000 Euro outcome as more favorable or decisive; instead, they downplay it in favor of likelihood. There is no indication that the individual compared the 'least probable outcomes' in the way the reason does, nor did they base their choice on which lottery offers a more favorable rare outcome. On the contrary, they chose A over B, while the reason would choose B. The information considered (probabilities of winning) partially overlaps, but the rule used (higher chance of non-zero vs more favorable rare outcome) is different. Therefore, the individual did not use this decision reason.",
